  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nLab\nshader-notes\n\n// Experiment\n\nshader-notes \n\nForty small WebGL sketches, each one under fifty lines and explained line by line.\n\nView the repo\nstars\n320\nlicense\nCC BY 4.0\nInstall\nCopy\nnpx degit sorenhale/shader-notes\n\n\nREADME.md\nCC BY 4.0\n\nForty small WebGL sketches. Each one is under fifty lines and every line has a comment, because I keep this notebook to stay honest about what I actually understand.\n\nA page from it\nglsl\nCopy\n// 07: soft circle\n\nprecision mediump float;\n\nuniform vec2 u_res;\n\n\n\nvoid main() {\n\n  vec2 p = (gl_FragCoord.xy * 2.0 - u_res) / u_res.y; // centre, keep the aspect\n\n  float d = length(p) - 0.5;                           // distance to a circle\n\n  float a = smoothstep(0.01, -0.01, d);                // one pixel of softness\n\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(vec3(a), 1.0);\n\n}\n\nWhat is in it\nNoise, from value noise to fractal sums\nSigned distance fields and how to combine them\nLighting with three numbers\nA few happy accidents, kept because they taught me something\n\nEvery sketch runs in the browser with a slider for each uniform.\n\nIn this readme\n\n01\nA page from it\n02\nWhat is in it\nKind\nExperiment\nLicense\nCC BY 4.0\nRepository\ngithub.com\nMore from the lab. \n06\nEverything in the lab\nLibrary · 2,140 stars\nuse-latency\nA React hook that measures how long every interaction really takes, in production.\nExperiment · 1,260 stars\nglyphfield\nDraws any picture as source code on a canvas. It runs the portrait at the top of this site.\nLibrary · 890 stars\ntinyflip\nLayout animations in 1.1 kB, using the FLIP technique and nothing else.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
